# Image TODO: hami-architecture-components-v1.png

## Purpose
Open the lesson with a single picture of HAMi's four components on a Kubernetes
cluster, making clear up front that the device-plugin is OFF in this lesson and
that HAMi is CNCF Incubating.

## Composition breakdown
- Left: a vertical stack of three component cards — "HAMi scheduler", "HAMi
  mutating webhook", "HAMi device-plugin (OFF in this lesson)". The device-plugin
  card is greyed out with a dashed border.
- Center: a Kubernetes API server box connected to the scheduler and webhook.
- Right: a worker node card with a green GPU chip labeled "nvidia.com/gpu (from
  fake-gpu-operator)" and two small pod boxes each tagged "gpumem" and "gpucores".
- Footer banner: "HAMi = scheduler + webhook + device-plugin + in-container core —
  software GPU sharing, no driver changes".
- Top-right: a small "CNCF Incubating" badge.
- Arrows: thin blue/elbow lines from API server to scheduler and webhook; from the
  node to the pods.
- Status colors: device-plugin card muted/dashed (disabled), everything else active.

## Gemini prompt
Create a flat technical architecture diagram titled "HAMi components on Kubernetes".
On the left, stack three rounded-rectangle component cards labeled "HAMi scheduler",
"HAMi mutating webhook", and "HAMi device-plugin (OFF in this lesson)"; grey out the
device-plugin card and give it a dashed border. In the center, draw a Kubernetes API
server box connected by thin elbow arrows to the scheduler and webhook cards. On the
right, draw a worker node card containing a bright green GPU chip labeled
"nvidia.com/gpu (from fake-gpu-operator)" and two small pod boxes each tagged "gpumem"
and "gpucores". Add a footer banner reading "HAMi = scheduler + webhook + device-plugin
+ in-container core — software GPU sharing, no driver changes" and a small "CNCF
Incubating" badge in the top-right corner. Style: flat technical illustration, dark navy
background (#0D1117), electric blue (#2F81F7) and neon green (#39D353) accents, off-white
(#E6EDF3) labels, subtle hexagonal grid texture at 10% opacity, no photorealism, no
gradients on solid elements, clean sans-serif labels, developer education platform
aesthetic. Aspect ratio 16:9.
